    'Qwen3.8Max(Max)V1': "This offline Canvas2D build solves ellipses using measured eccentricities and periods, with a moving belt, pan, zoom, focus, and follow. Display semimajor axes, orientations, and initial phases are custom and have no real epoch; only orbital criteria deduct these. The Moon is a periodic screen-space ellipse with half-quality illustrative credit. The object called Halley uses e=.86 and custom planar orientation/phase, so it is not genuine Halley and does not become an other-comet bonus. Rings and atmospheres are 2D illustrations, there is no Bloom/ACES, and pause works without a full reset. Canvas2D and visual appearance carry no extra penalties.",
