    'MiniMax_M3_thinking-1': "Eight planets have focused ellipses, Newton Kepler solving and approximate eccentricities/periods, but random nodes/phases. The entity transform places an in-plane component on the vertical axis while paths remain in another plane, so they do not match. Rings lack shadows and there is no main belt. Bloom/OutputPass ACES work; atmospheres are rims. The Moon omits a factor of two pi and uses the wrong frame and is invalid. Spins are arbitrary visual rates. Focus/follow only steer the target; zoom is safe. Setting the ordinary speed slider to 0.5 produces zero times Infinity, poisoning time and positions with NaN. Runtime reproduction confirms L2, which marks T4 without a score cap. Pause leaves spin running and reset does not repair the NaN speed. Half-float postprocessing has no fallback or scene MSAA. The low-speed NaN input fault is charged once under runtime3; Kepler solving stays stable for finite inputs, so numerical stability remains1.",
