    'GLM_5_1_high-1': {"title":"Solar System Motion Model","note":"Online Three.js uses Sun-focused ellipses with approximate periods and eccentricities, but advances the parameter angle uniformly without Kepler solving, orbital nodes or an epoch. Paths and entities share geometry. The asteroid belt is static; Bloom works and ACES is partially applied, rings have no physical shadows and there is no planetary atmosphere. The Moon inherits Earth’s tilted spinning mesh and is invalid. Venus and Uranus combine flipped axes with negative spin, reducing data accuracy. Focus and continuous camera follow work; pause stops only planet revolution while planet and Moon rotation continue, and there is no complete reset. Half-float postprocessing has no fallback or scene MSAA. Actual UnrealBloomPass output tone-maps the base image through MeshBasicMaterial, then adds Bloom without mapping the combined result; ACES receives0.4 partial credit.","issue":""},
